      en: "Lake Ghoubbet is a hypersaline lake located in central Djibouti, about 20 km southwest of Djibouti City. It covers an area of 50 km² with a maximum depth of 20 meters. Salinity levels exceed 300 ppt, making it one of the saltiest lakes in the world. The lake is surrounded by volcanic hills and basalt flows. It supports a unique ecosystem of halophilic bacteria and algae, giving the water a reddish hue. The lake is an important site for migratory waterbirds, including greater flamingos (Phoenicopterus roseus) and various tern species. Salt extraction occurs on the lake's edges.",
